Besides needing to convert coordinates from tile to canvas (maybe at `SliceInk::inkHline`?), there's a further issue that arises uppon adding `&& !params.ink->isSlice()` to the check here:

https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/0f7cac0f0cc93a9a1e06afe5fef3fd641c92eb3b/src/app/ui/editor/tool_loop_impl.cpp#L761-L768

When making a new slice in tiles mode, nothing is drawn to indicate the area being sliced, and at times, a segfault is thrown on my end.

Looking at the coredump, the crash happens at `XorInkProcessing<RgbTraits>::processPixel`, both pointers being dereferenced (`m_dstAddress` and `m_srcAddress`) are invalid from what I can see.

But I can't reproduce this with selection tools, whose ink has the same base class and uses the same ink processing, so I'm assuming the actual problem has to be elsewhere. I'm reading `src/app/tools/intertwine.cpp` and `src/app/tools/point_shape.cpp` to see if I can find anything.

